Based on your preference for a simple, reliable slow cooker, the recommendations are the Presto Nomad 6-Quart Slow Cooker and the West Bend 6-Quart Manual Slow Cooker. Both models offer easy-to-use features, with simple temperature settings and removable inserts for serving. However, please note that the West Bend slow cooker has dishwasher-safe parts, while the Presto model excels in its portable design, making it ideal for potlucks and travel.

For a more advanced option with a variety of cooking functions, you may want to consider the Philips Viva Collection All-in-One Multicooker if it becomes more readily available. But if you prefer the simplicity described, the Presto Nomad 6-Quart Slow Cooker and West Bend 6-Quart Manual Slow Cooker would be the best recommendations to start with.
